WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.400 --> 01:34.950
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.289 --> 01:37.720
[Episode 34]

4
01:38.640 --> 01:39.759
Instead of hesitating

5
01:38.740 --> 01:41.820
[Headquarters of the Central Military Commission, Anshunchang Ferry, Sichuan]

6
01:39.920 --> 01:41.039
and pacing back and forth,

7
01:41.039 --> 01:42.479
we might as well face the difficulties head-on.

8
01:42.479 --> 01:43.789
Stubbornly holding Anshunchang

9
01:43.789 --> 01:46.120
would make us the Shi Dakai of 72 years ago.

10
01:46.350 --> 01:48.870
Our idea is to divide our forces into 2 routes.

11
01:48.870 --> 01:51.130
The left column and the right column will act simultaneously,

12
01:51.130 --> 01:53.530
to capture Luding Bridge and then reunite.

13
01:54.190 --> 01:57.220
Let's deploy the 1st Red Division and the Military Commission Cadre Regiment

14
01:57.220 --> 01:57.620
as the right column.

15
01:57.620 --> 01:59.080
You two will take command.

16
01:59.780 --> 02:02.060
After crossing the river at Anshunchang,

17
02:02.060 --> 02:04.010
advance north along the east bank.

18
02:05.310 --> 02:06.860
The headquarters of the 1st Red Army Corps,

19
02:06.860 --> 02:08.979
the main force of the 2nd Division, and the 5th Red Army Corps

20
02:08.979 --> 02:09.110
will form the left column

21
02:09.110 --> 02:10.310
under Lin Biao's command

22
02:10.310 --> 02:12.590
and advance north along the west bank of the Dadu River.

23
02:12.590 --> 02:14.690
The Military Commission Column and the rest of the troops

24
02:14.690 --> 02:16.660
will move with the left column.

25
02:18.240 --> 02:19.400
If

26
02:19.870 --> 02:21.490
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army Corps]

27
02:21.490 --> 02:23.120
[and Political Commissar of the Central Red Army Advance Force]

28
02:21.660 --> 02:23.870
Luding Bridge has already been destroyed by the enemy,

29
02:23.870 --> 02:25.640
even if we arrive on time,

30
02:25.660 --> 02:28.720
the left and right columns won't be able to join forces.

31
02:43.310 --> 02:46.470
Then we'll have to operate on opposite sides of the river.

32
02:46.470 --> 02:48.430
You will fight a guerrilla war in western Sichuan,

33
02:48.430 --> 02:51.960
and we will fight a guerrilla war on the Sichuan-Xikang border.

34
02:52.220 --> 02:54.079
This is the worst-case scenario.

35
03:33.320 --> 03:34.320
Corps Commander.

36
03:39.750 --> 03:40.310
Report.

37
03:40.380 --> 03:41.100
Speak.

38
03:41.510 --> 03:42.640
Urgent telegram from the Military Commission.

39
03:42.250 --> 03:45.300
[Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army Corps]

40
03:45.370 --> 03:47.200
[Zuo Quan, Chief of Staff of the 1st Red Army Corps]

41
03:48.780 --> 03:49.820
Map.

42
03:57.060 --> 03:59.660
Which regiment should we send as the vanguard?

43
04:00.030 --> 04:01.030
Of course,

44
04:01.780 --> 04:02.780
the 4th Regiment.

45
04:09.710 --> 04:10.590
Company Commander.

46
04:10.590 --> 04:11.910
What does Luding Bridge look like?

47
04:11.910 --> 04:12.780
What else would a bridge look like?

48
04:12.780 --> 04:13.770
Bridgeheads on both sides,

49
04:13.770 --> 04:14.910
and piers in the middle.

50
04:14.910 --> 04:16.310
160 kilometers in 3 days.

51
04:16.339 --> 04:17.220
What are you muttering about?

52
04:17.220 --> 04:17.779
Company Commander.

53
04:17.779 --> 04:19.839
This is nothing for our 4th Regiment.

54
04:23.100 --> 04:23.540
Grab me.

55
04:23.540 --> 04:24.150
Hurry!

56
04:25.460 --> 04:26.270
Is everything okay ahead?

57
04:26.270 --> 04:26.860
Come on!

58
04:27.180 --> 04:27.980
Pull up!

59
04:27.980 --> 04:29.510
One, two, three!

60
04:29.740 --> 04:31.270
One, two, three!

61
04:31.740 --> 04:33.270
One, two, three!

62
04:33.590 --> 04:34.300
Be careful.

63
04:34.510 --> 04:35.630
Comrades, stay safe.

64
04:35.630 --> 04:36.830
Everyone, be careful.

65
04:36.830 --> 04:37.960
Watch your step too.

66
04:38.110 --> 04:38.909
Let's go.

67
04:41.150 --> 04:42.150
Take cover!

68
04:44.800 --> 04:45.630
Take cover!

69
04:46.450 --> 04:47.909
Company Commander, you're injured.

70
04:47.909 --> 04:49.070
Take cover quickly.

71
04:51.510 --> 04:52.300
Medic!

72
04:52.909 --> 04:53.510
Here!

73
04:53.600 --> 04:55.530
Our Company Commander is injured.

74
04:58.950 --> 05:01.180
Company Commander, why are there still enemies?

75
05:01.180 --> 05:03.910
Nonsense. You think all we have to do is marching?

76
05:04.510 --> 05:06.510
Company Commander, does it hurt?

77
05:06.590 --> 05:09.380
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

78
05:07.180 --> 05:08.150
Brat,

79
05:08.360 --> 05:09.770
hold back your tears.

80
05:10.300 --> 05:11.230
What's the rush?

81
05:11.590 --> 05:12.520
It's no big deal.

82
05:12.740 --> 05:14.300
Red Army soldiers don't shed tears.

83
05:14.300 --> 05:15.190
Hold them back.

84
05:18.020 --> 05:20.890
Brat, I didn't care for you in vain.

85
05:30.660 --> 05:31.510
We have to take a detour.

86
05:31.510 --> 05:32.970
Comrades, into the woods.

87
05:33.030 --> 05:35.000
Take cover and go up the mountain. Hurry.

88
05:35.000 --> 05:35.670
Hurry!

89
05:35.980 --> 05:37.180
Move up the mountain!

90
05:43.270 --> 05:44.590
Let's go.

91
06:46.310 --> 06:50.510
Is the vanguard planning to march day and night without eating or sleeping?

92
06:52.940 --> 06:55.350
[Huang Guifa and Wu Yue'e: A Happy Marriage for a Hundred Years]

93
07:29.740 --> 07:30.590
Staff Officer Zhang.

94
07:30.590 --> 07:31.540
Vice Chairman Zhou.

95
07:31.540 --> 07:32.340
Tell the comrades

96
07:32.340 --> 07:33.470
to work a bit harder.

97
07:33.470 --> 07:35.100
Take all these supplies with you.

98
07:35.100 --> 07:36.710
Don't leave anything behind.

99
07:36.710 --> 07:37.909
When the battle is over,

100
07:37.909 --> 07:39.030
they must be returned to the 4th Regiment.

101
07:39.030 --> 07:39.659
Yes, sir.

102
07:40.300 --> 07:41.390
Third Squad, step forward.

103
07:41.390 --> 07:42.470
Here!

104
07:42.470 --> 07:43.630
Take all the supplies.

105
07:43.630 --> 07:45.690
Not a single piece should be missing.

106
07:58.300 --> 07:59.070
Watch your step.

107
07:59.070 --> 07:59.630
Okay.

108
08:00.000 --> 08:00.450
Come on.

109
08:00.450 --> 08:02.540
Come on, move up.

110
08:06.540 --> 08:07.000
Move up.

111
08:08.390 --> 08:08.910
Are you okay?

112
08:08.910 --> 08:09.740
Careful.

113
08:10.270 --> 08:11.060
Careful, comrades.

114
08:11.060 --> 08:12.070
Come on, watch your step.

115
08:12.070 --> 08:12.590
Watch your step.

116
08:12.590 --> 08:13.520
Come on, move up.

117
08:13.830 --> 08:14.270
Careful.

118
08:14.270 --> 08:14.730
Move up.

119
08:14.860 --> 08:16.060
Regiment Commander.

120
08:16.070 --> 08:16.540
Political Commissar.

121
08:16.540 --> 08:17.210
Is your hand okay?

122
08:17.210 --> 08:17.470
It's fine.

123
08:17.470 --> 08:17.800
Good.

124
08:17.830 --> 08:18.360
Let's go.

125
08:18.630 --> 08:19.180
Let's go.

126
08:19.740 --> 08:20.510
Move up.

127
08:21.630 --> 08:22.540
Keep up.

128
08:22.770 --> 08:23.700
Watch your step.

129
08:24.390 --> 08:25.180
Come on.

130
08:26.080 --> 08:26.710
Come on.

131
08:27.220 --> 08:27.780
Come on.

132
08:28.340 --> 08:28.860
Move up.

133
09:17.180 --> 09:18.030
Chairman Mao.

134
09:18.180 --> 09:18.990
Camping is canceled.

135
09:18.990 --> 09:20.540
The cook didn't have time to make food,

136
09:20.540 --> 09:21.580
so he just boiled some water.

137
09:21.580 --> 09:22.580
Please have some.

138
09:28.170 --> 09:29.910
Chairman, please change into cloth shoes.

139
09:29.910 --> 09:31.840
Your feet are covered in blisters.

140
09:38.270 --> 09:39.750
Chairman, I still have some dry rations here.

141
09:39.750 --> 09:41.150
Please eat some.

142
10:06.230 --> 10:09.200
[Chengdu, Sichuan]

143
10:09.750 --> 10:12.010
Seeing the two of you united in good faith

144
10:12.270 --> 10:13.670
brings me great comfort.

145
10:13.910 --> 10:15.750
Generalissimo, with you taking charge,

146
10:15.750 --> 10:17.110
we should naturally eliminate our differences

147
10:17.110 --> 10:18.230
and unite against the enemy.

148
10:18.230 --> 10:19.430
Ziqian (Liu Wenhui).

149
10:19.780 --> 10:20.640
What do you say?

150
10:22.910 --> 10:24.940
We're both Lius, after all.

151
10:25.270 --> 10:26.150
Good.

152
10:26.390 --> 10:28.180
As long as Sichuan is stable,

153
10:28.940 --> 10:30.600
the southwest will be secure.

154
10:33.000 --> 10:33.760
[Liu Wenhui, Commander-in-Chief of the Sichuan-Xikang Border Defense Army of the Kuomintang]

155
10:33.760 --> 10:34.520
[and Commander of the 24th Army]

156
10:34.520 --> 10:35.430
[Liu Xiang, Kuomintang Commander-in-Chief of the Sichuan Campaign to Suppress the Communists]

157
10:35.430 --> 10:36.350
[and Chairman of the Sichuan Provincial Government]

158
10:43.180 --> 10:44.910
Generalissimo Chiang is here!

159
10:48.700 --> 10:49.580
Gentlemen.

160
10:49.910 --> 10:51.510
My visit to Chengdu this time

161
10:51.990 --> 10:54.190
is only partly to supervise the battle.

162
10:54.230 --> 10:56.420
There is an even more important matter,

163
10:56.420 --> 10:57.580
which is that I want

164
10:57.940 --> 11:00.300
to congratulate Fucheng (Liu Xiang)

165
11:00.460 --> 11:03.390
on his appointment as Chairman of Sichuan Province.

166
11:11.150 --> 11:12.680
Thank you, Generalissimo.

167
11:12.780 --> 11:14.700
That I am where I am today

168
11:14.940 --> 11:17.110
is entirely due to your cultivation.

169
11:21.300 --> 11:22.270
Chairman Liu.

170
11:22.910 --> 11:26.910
The Generalissimo's congratulations are not just verbal.

171
11:27.110 --> 11:29.820
He has brought you a great gift.

172
11:30.230 --> 11:31.750
He knows that your previous

173
11:31.750 --> 11:33.820
six-pronged attack on Xu Xiangqian's troops

174
11:33.820 --> 11:34.990
caused significant losses.

175
11:34.990 --> 11:36.250
He specially instructed

176
11:36.250 --> 11:37.730
to provide money and guns,

177
11:38.030 --> 11:41.230
and to help you establish a military and political school

178
11:41.380 --> 11:43.500
to train talents.

179
11:45.520 --> 11:48.890
Generalissimo, I am deeply grateful.

180
11:50.600 --> 11:53.530
Generalissimo, I'll drink first to show my respect.

181
12:04.150 --> 12:04.910
Everyone.

182
12:06.300 --> 12:08.420
The Generalissimo has come to Sichuan to supervise the battle.

183
12:08.420 --> 12:10.700
I should do my duty as a host.

184
12:11.180 --> 12:13.300
I have prepared some Sichuan dishes

185
12:13.630 --> 12:14.610
and a cup of wine.

186
12:14.910 --> 12:16.970
Please have a taste, Generalissimo.

187
12:17.420 --> 12:18.060
Good.

188
12:18.660 --> 12:19.340
Please.

189
12:59.710 --> 13:00.630
Chairman Liu.

190
13:00.990 --> 13:03.450
The Generalissimo can't handle spicy food.

191
13:04.040 --> 13:05.110
Generalissimo.

192
13:05.590 --> 13:07.190
You can't handle spicy food.

193
13:07.680 --> 13:08.880
Here is some vinegar.

194
13:09.700 --> 13:11.700
Vinegar can relieve the spiciness.

195
13:13.830 --> 13:14.280
Okay.

196
13:14.300 --> 13:15.020
Someone.

197
13:16.100 --> 13:17.670
Bring the prepared

198
13:17.750 --> 13:19.180
Fenghua-style dishes

199
13:19.390 --> 13:20.650
to the Generalissimo.

200
13:21.370 --> 13:22.520
No need. No need.

201
13:22.910 --> 13:24.030
Fucheng,

202
13:25.060 --> 13:26.190
I remember

203
13:27.580 --> 13:29.940
Du Fu wrote a five-character-per-line poem,

204
13:29.940 --> 13:32.740
"Three Playful Poems for the Prince of Hanzhong".

205
13:32.910 --> 13:34.330
There is a line in it:

206
13:35.390 --> 13:37.420
"Shu wine is unrivaled in richness,

207
13:38.060 --> 13:40.630
And the river fish are a delicacy worth seeking."

208
13:40.630 --> 13:42.180
Since I am here,

209
13:42.300 --> 13:43.910
I am willing to join everyone

210
13:44.350 --> 13:47.350
to savor the flavors of Sichuan.

211
13:52.540 --> 13:54.660
Generalissimo, you have a great memory.

212
13:54.660 --> 13:55.900
I admire you.

213
13:56.300 --> 13:57.230
Generalissimo.

214
13:57.350 --> 14:00.030
This dish is made with fresh river fish that are in season.

215
14:00.030 --> 14:00.990
Please try it.

216
14:02.990 --> 14:03.940
Okay.

217
14:15.820 --> 14:17.780
You don't all have to look at me.

218
14:18.060 --> 14:19.660
You can start eating too,

219
14:20.060 --> 14:20.660
right?

220
14:21.230 --> 14:22.540
Come on, let's eat.

221
14:23.630 --> 14:24.350
Okay.

222
14:31.010 --> 14:31.740
Someone.

223
14:32.940 --> 14:34.110
Change the Generalissimo's water.

224
14:34.110 --> 14:34.870
Yes, sir.

225
14:41.660 --> 14:42.450
Report!

226
14:42.480 --> 14:43.410
Generalissimo.

227
14:46.530 --> 14:48.110
Commander, urgent telegram.

228
14:48.110 --> 14:50.300
Generalissimo, allow me to offer you a toast as well.

229
14:50.300 --> 14:52.300
I'll drink first to show my respect.

230
14:56.870 --> 14:57.930
What is it?

231
14:58.780 --> 14:59.780
Tell me.

232
15:02.510 --> 15:03.580
Report, Generalissimo.

233
15:03.580 --> 15:06.110
According to aerial reconnaissance reports,

234
15:06.110 --> 15:08.020
this morning, the Zhu-Mao Communist Army

235
15:08.020 --> 15:09.150
had some troops

236
15:09.390 --> 15:12.800
cross the Dadu River from Anshunchang.

237
15:12.890 --> 15:15.320
They have currently reached the Anqingba area.

238
15:15.320 --> 15:17.820
The rest of the main force is advancing rapidly along the west bank

239
15:17.820 --> 15:20.190
towards Luding Bridge.

240
15:25.780 --> 15:28.940
It seems Mao Zedong is not Shi Dakai.

241
15:30.230 --> 15:31.760
He still knows how to adapt.

242
15:32.300 --> 15:33.430
Northeast of Luding

243
15:33.940 --> 15:35.270
is Tianquan and Lushan.

244
15:35.390 --> 15:37.110
Once Zhu and Mao break through there,

245
15:37.110 --> 15:38.630
it will be very difficult to stop

246
15:38.630 --> 15:41.630
them from joining forces with Xu Xiangqian's troops.

247
15:41.990 --> 15:43.050
Blow up the bridge.

248
15:43.510 --> 15:44.870
Blow up Luding Bridge.

249
15:45.740 --> 15:48.280
This way, we can block most of the Communist Army

250
15:48.280 --> 15:50.610
on the west bank of the Dadu River.

251
15:50.870 --> 15:53.270
The small number of the Communist Army that has crossed the river

252
15:53.270 --> 15:54.930
won't be able to achieve much.

253
15:56.270 --> 15:57.820
It shouldn't come to this.

254
15:58.270 --> 16:00.420
This bridge was built during the Kangxi era

255
16:00.420 --> 16:02.870
at a cost of over 40,000 taels of silver.

256
16:03.080 --> 16:06.210
It has been a vital route connecting Sichuan and Xikang since ancient times.

257
16:06.210 --> 16:07.340
Once it's blown up,

258
16:07.780 --> 16:10.460
travel between Sichuan and Xikang will be impossible.

259
16:10.460 --> 16:12.920
This concerns the livelihood of the people.

260
16:13.350 --> 16:16.230
Uncle, the people's livelihood is indeed important,

261
16:16.230 --> 16:19.420
but annihilating the communists is imminent.

262
16:20.030 --> 16:21.120
Which is more important?

263
16:21.120 --> 16:23.400
Uncle, you need to think it through.

264
16:32.020 --> 16:32.950
Generalissimo.

265
16:33.030 --> 16:34.510
I will go to Hanyuan to supervise the battle right away,

266
16:34.510 --> 16:36.060
and urgently dispatch troops to reinforce Luding

267
16:36.060 --> 16:38.390
to ensure Luding Bridge is fully secured.

268
16:38.630 --> 16:39.910
Ziqian (Liu Wenhui).

269
16:44.390 --> 16:46.230
Sichuan is your hometown.

270
16:48.460 --> 16:51.990
You should know its terrain, its waterways, and its people.

271
16:52.420 --> 16:55.300
The Communist Army is just fleeing here.

272
16:55.990 --> 16:57.660
I bet they can't

273
16:57.940 --> 16:59.940
outrun your car.

274
17:00.990 --> 17:01.870
So,

275
17:03.550 --> 17:07.200
you still have time to drink this glass of wine.

276
17:10.260 --> 17:10.829
Yes, sir.

277
17:12.240 --> 17:14.240
I heard there's a saying in Sichuan.

278
17:14.869 --> 17:16.730
"A true hero can take the numbing,

279
17:16.910 --> 17:19.589
and a real man can take the heat."

280
17:20.180 --> 17:21.180
So today,

281
17:21.390 --> 17:22.790
I will do as the Romans do.

282
17:23.150 --> 17:24.390
Like all of you,

283
17:25.390 --> 17:27.190
I'll be a true hero and a real man.

284
17:28.270 --> 17:29.940
-Great! -Great!

285
17:32.870 --> 17:33.570
Come on.

286
17:35.790 --> 17:36.720
Generalissimo.

287
17:36.770 --> 17:40.050
I thank you for treating the men of the Sichuan Army

288
17:40.070 --> 17:41.600
as your comrades-in-arms.

289
17:41.800 --> 17:43.040
Fucheng.

290
17:44.220 --> 17:46.180
You wear the symbol of the Party on your chest.

291
17:45.220 --> 17:47.550
[Liu Xiang, General, Commander-in-Chief of the Sichuan Campaign to Suppress the Communists,]

292
17:46.630 --> 17:49.460
I, too, will hold you all in my heart.

293
17:47.550 --> 17:49.890
[Military Affairs Commission of the National Government]

294
17:50.460 --> 17:53.420
First internal pacification, then external resistance.

295
17:53.420 --> 17:54.790
If the Communist Army is not eliminated,

296
17:54.790 --> 17:56.120
I cannot sleep at night.

297
17:56.660 --> 17:57.870
So I hope

298
17:58.110 --> 18:00.740
that under Chairman Liu's leadership, all of you

299
18:00.740 --> 18:01.790
can properly

300
18:02.980 --> 18:05.040
live up to the 4 characters behind me.

301
18:06.100 --> 18:06.880
Alright?

302
18:14.070 --> 18:15.790
Please rest assured, Generalissimo.

303
18:15.790 --> 18:17.500
The Chung-cheng Sword you gave me

304
18:17.500 --> 18:19.590
is always hanging over my head.

305
18:19.680 --> 18:20.250
Good.

306
18:22.180 --> 18:22.860
Then,

307
18:25.310 --> 18:27.260
I'm counting on all of you.

308
18:58.360 --> 19:00.160
Just wipe out the Communist Army

309
19:00.310 --> 19:02.310
on the banks of the Dadu River.

310
19:02.700 --> 19:03.710
Yes, sir!

311
19:05.120 --> 19:09.120
[West Bank of the Dadu River, Sichuan]

312
19:15.940 --> 19:16.630
Report.

313
19:16.870 --> 19:19.800
The Second Bureau has just cracked a coded telegram.

314
19:22.420 --> 19:23.870
Enlai, what's the situation?

315
19:23.870 --> 19:25.310
The enemy has sent the 4th Brigade of the Sichuan Army

316
19:25.310 --> 19:26.510
to reinforce Luding.

317
19:30.630 --> 19:31.630
It seems now

318
19:31.980 --> 19:33.910
that the enemy is closer to Luding.

319
19:33.980 --> 19:34.980
They are taking the main road,

320
19:34.980 --> 19:36.910
so they will be much faster than us.

321
19:37.180 --> 19:38.690
The 1st Division on the east bank

322
19:38.690 --> 19:39.670
encountered resistance at Wajiaoba

323
19:39.670 --> 19:41.220
from the 5th Brigade of the Sichuan Army.

324
19:41.220 --> 19:43.350
I'm afraid it will be hard for them to reach Luding in a short time.

325
19:43.350 --> 19:44.070
The key

326
19:44.550 --> 19:46.180
is the 4th Regiment on the west bank.

327
19:46.180 --> 19:48.110
The 4th Regiment was also held up

328
19:48.260 --> 19:49.740
by enemy forces at Pusagang yesterday.

329
19:49.740 --> 19:51.070
They advanced a total of 40 kilometers,

330
19:51.070 --> 19:52.390
and are still 120 kilometers away

331
19:52.390 --> 19:54.020
from Luding Bridge.

332
19:55.280 --> 19:57.630
Our Red Army will never be Shi Dakai.

333
19:59.180 --> 19:59.980
Tell Lin Biao,

334
20:00.390 --> 20:01.700
no matter what difficulties they encounter,

335
20:01.700 --> 20:02.630
the 4th Regiment

336
20:02.700 --> 20:05.180
must arrive at Luding Bridge

337
20:05.550 --> 20:06.880
before 6 a.m. tomorrow.

338
20:07.910 --> 20:10.370
Even if they have to fly, they must get there.

339
20:16.650 --> 20:17.410
Yang,

340
20:17.830 --> 20:19.110
after marching for so long,

341
20:19.110 --> 20:20.170
are your legs okay?

342
20:20.260 --> 20:21.110
It's fine.

343
20:21.350 --> 20:22.480
Getting there is more important.

344
20:22.480 --> 20:23.020
Okay.

345
20:24.910 --> 20:26.020
Regiment Commander Huang,

346
20:26.020 --> 20:27.430
Political Commissar Yang.

347
20:27.430 --> 20:28.270
What's wrong?

348
20:32.340 --> 20:34.670
An urgent order from the Corps Commander.

349
20:43.260 --> 20:44.220
Comrades!

350
20:44.980 --> 20:46.830
A telegram from the Military Commission.

351
20:46.830 --> 20:49.420
It says you are heroes on the front line

352
20:49.520 --> 20:51.320
and models in the Red Army.

353
20:52.150 --> 20:54.150
Brave soldiers of the 4th Regiment,

354
20:54.790 --> 20:57.590
the 5th Regiment once set a record

355
20:55.750 --> 20:59.750
[Huang Kaixiang, Commander of the 4th Regiment]

356
20:57.830 --> 20:59.890
of marching 80 kilometers in one day.

357
20:59.980 --> 21:01.550
As the vanguard,

358
21:01.980 --> 21:03.220
I ask you now,

359
21:03.550 --> 21:05.110
can you break this record?

360
21:05.390 --> 21:08.110
Yes! Yes! Yes!

361
21:08.230 --> 21:08.910
Good.

362
21:09.040 --> 21:11.100
Comrades, speed up!

363
21:13.790 --> 21:15.520
This is the most thrilling page

364
21:15.750 --> 21:18.150
in the history of the Red Army's Long March,

365
21:18.980 --> 21:21.550
and a miracle in human military history.

366
21:22.320 --> 21:24.590
One day and night, two legs,

367
21:25.070 --> 21:26.830
and 120 kilometers.

368
21:27.390 --> 21:29.460
The 4th Regiment, racing against time,

369
21:29.460 --> 21:31.700
running on the track of destiny,

370
21:32.590 --> 21:35.770
created an unprecedented record of human endurance.

371
21:37.110 --> 21:38.550
Just as Marshal Nie Rongzhen

372
21:38.550 --> 21:40.460
later recalled,

373
21:40.790 --> 21:43.110
"Although the situation was dangerous at that time,

374
21:43.110 --> 21:45.390
we finally succeeded.

375
21:45.590 --> 21:47.220
It was indeed hard-won,

376
21:47.790 --> 21:49.550
but by no means accidental.

377
21:49.980 --> 21:51.710
In our struggle against the Kuomintang,

378
21:51.710 --> 21:53.430
we were often one step ahead,

379
21:53.480 --> 21:55.140
taking the enemy by surprise.

380
21:55.250 --> 21:55.930
This was because

381
21:55.930 --> 21:59.190
we were the Workers' and Peasants' Red Army, led by the CPC,

382
21:59.210 --> 22:01.820
with a level of political commitment

383
22:01.870 --> 22:03.040
our enemies could never match

384
22:03.040 --> 22:04.250
and the tactical skill to outmaneuver

385
22:04.250 --> 22:07.070
superior forces through flexible, mobile tactics.

386
22:07.070 --> 22:09.220
Above all, our officers and soldiers possessed

387
22:09.220 --> 22:12.070
a spirit of self-sacrifice, remaining utterly loyal

388
22:12.070 --> 22:15.510
to the Party, to the people, and to the Chinese revolution.

389
22:16.110 --> 22:19.050
That was why we could sometimes turn the tide in seemingly hopeless situations,

390
22:19.050 --> 22:23.390
raise the banner of victory once more, and secure victory again."

391
22:26.720 --> 22:27.590
Hurry up over there.

392
22:27.590 --> 22:28.850
Remove them! Quickly!

393
22:29.830 --> 22:31.230
Hurry up and remove them.

394
22:31.980 --> 22:33.190
Guys, hurry up!

395
22:36.660 --> 22:37.860
Pull then up quickly!

396
22:42.660 --> 22:43.520
Get up quickly!

397
22:44.590 --> 22:45.420
Hurry up!

398
22:48.500 --> 22:49.430
Grab them and go!

399
22:51.400 --> 22:52.230
Hurry up!

400
22:59.130 --> 23:00.010
Hurry up!

401
23:04.440 --> 23:06.020
Comrades, hold on to the rope.

402
23:06.020 --> 23:07.370
Take turns resting at intervals.

403
23:07.370 --> 23:09.700
Keep your eyes on the incense light ahead.

404
23:09.870 --> 23:11.110
Stay close to the mountain.

405
23:11.110 --> 23:12.390
Watch out for the cliff.

406
23:12.390 --> 23:13.700
No torches allowed.

407
23:14.020 --> 23:15.390
Don't fall behind.

408
23:16.660 --> 23:18.320
Comrades, hold on to the rope.

409
23:18.590 --> 23:20.450
Take turns resting at intervals.

410
23:20.790 --> 23:22.190
Hang in there, comrades.

411
23:22.500 --> 23:23.250
Hold on a little longer.

412
23:23.250 --> 23:24.310
Don't fall asleep.

413
23:24.710 --> 23:25.380
Wake up.

414
23:39.190 --> 23:40.060
Come on.

415
23:40.730 --> 23:41.880
Be careful.

416
23:43.640 --> 23:45.500
Take turns resting at intervals.

417
23:55.630 --> 23:57.150
Come on, stay awake.

418
24:11.080 --> 24:11.990
Hurry up!

419
24:13.500 --> 24:15.960
Regiment Commander, Political Commissar.

420
24:18.390 --> 24:19.480
Regiment Commander, Political Commissar.

421
24:19.480 --> 24:20.940
Look at the opposite bank.

422
24:22.420 --> 24:24.020
Hurry up, hurry up!

423
24:24.550 --> 24:26.500
As long as we stop the Communist Army,

424
24:26.500 --> 24:27.910
we'll have money

425
24:28.390 --> 24:30.220
and opium!

426
24:30.590 --> 24:31.740
Hurry up!

427
24:31.970 --> 24:35.230
The Sichuan Army is definitely heading for Luding Bridge.

428
24:35.480 --> 24:36.750
They have torches to light the way.

429
24:36.750 --> 24:38.150
We are moving in the dark.

430
24:38.630 --> 24:40.180
When will we get there?

431
24:40.700 --> 24:41.660
It's so far away.

432
24:41.690 --> 24:42.940
The enemy can't see clearly, either.

433
24:42.940 --> 24:44.540
Let's light our torches too.

434
24:45.180 --> 24:46.070
Good idea.

435
24:46.460 --> 24:47.350
Comrades!

436
24:47.630 --> 24:49.090
Light the torches, quick!

437
24:49.220 --> 24:50.250
Light the torches!

438
24:50.250 --> 24:50.840
Quick!

439
25:06.020 --> 25:08.350
Which unit are you from?

440
25:09.790 --> 25:11.120
Is anyone from Sichuan?

441
25:11.460 --> 25:12.110
Here!

442
25:14.840 --> 25:16.240
Reporting, I am.

443
25:16.260 --> 25:17.210
Shout to the opposite side.

444
25:17.210 --> 25:19.810
Say we encountered the Red Army and retreated.

445
25:20.220 --> 25:22.620
We encountered the Red Army and retreated!

446
25:25.740 --> 25:26.460
Keep up!

447
25:26.490 --> 25:27.650
Keep up in the back!

448
25:30.110 --> 25:31.020
Comrades!

449
25:31.390 --> 25:33.430
Double time! Double time!

450
25:33.580 --> 25:34.180
Quick!

451
26:40.790 --> 26:44.690
[Chengdu, Sichuan]

452
26:41.420 --> 26:42.350
This morning,

453
26:42.630 --> 26:43.630
Yoshijiro Umezu,

454
26:43.910 --> 26:46.740
as the commander of the Japanese Garrison Army in China,

455
26:46.740 --> 26:47.800
put pressure on us.

456
26:47.870 --> 26:49.310
Using the Hebei incident as an excuse,

457
26:49.310 --> 26:50.920
he wants to include Tianjin and Peiping

458
26:50.920 --> 26:52.450
in the demilitarized zone.

459
26:52.590 --> 26:53.450
Subsequently,

460
26:53.590 --> 26:56.210
Takashi Sakai, Chief of Staff of the Japanese Garrison Army,

461
26:56.210 --> 26:59.010
and Takahashi Tan, military attaché of the Japanese Embassy in China,

462
26:59.010 --> 27:01.220
met with Minister He Yingqin at Jurentang

463
27:01.220 --> 27:02.680
and made the same request.

464
27:02.700 --> 27:03.830
This He Yingqin...

465
27:04.070 --> 27:04.940
Negotiating, negotiating...

466
27:04.940 --> 27:06.600
How exactly did he negotiate?

467
27:07.220 --> 27:08.870
Things have come to this point.

468
27:08.870 --> 27:10.600
Why are you only telling me now?

469
27:12.590 --> 27:15.720
Is this the strategy for resisting foreign aggression?

470
27:16.260 --> 27:17.590
What about internal pacification?

471
27:17.590 --> 27:18.110
Yuanjing (He Guoguang).

472
27:18.110 --> 27:19.700
How is the situation on your side?

473
27:19.700 --> 27:21.070
Please rest assured, Generalissimo.

474
27:21.070 --> 27:22.830
The 38th Regiment of the 4th Brigade of the Sichuan Army

475
27:22.830 --> 27:24.790
arrived in Luding Town last night.

476
27:24.980 --> 27:26.380
The 11th Regiment also blocked

477
27:26.380 --> 27:28.630
the Communist forces crossing the river from Anshunchang at Tiesigou.

478
27:28.630 --> 27:29.910
Luding Bridge is impregnable.

479
27:29.910 --> 27:30.590
Good.

480
27:30.830 --> 27:31.830
The Luding Bridge

481
27:32.550 --> 27:33.590
must not be lost.

482
27:33.940 --> 27:34.550
Yes, sir!

483
27:36.110 --> 27:37.400
Keep up. Hurry up!

484
27:38.800 --> 27:40.040
Dress right, dress!

485
27:40.590 --> 27:41.700
Ready, front!

486
27:41.940 --> 27:42.790
At ease!

487
27:43.020 --> 27:44.030
Attention!

488
27:44.260 --> 27:45.540
Right face!

489
27:46.180 --> 27:47.790
Double time, march!

490
27:48.350 --> 27:50.070
The Red Army is about to attack.

491
27:50.070 --> 27:52.350
You must hold Luding Bridge!

492
27:52.910 --> 27:54.070
Yes, sir!

493
27:55.530 --> 27:57.110
Rest assured, Brigade Commander.

494
27:57.110 --> 27:58.630
I have ordered Zhou's Battalion

495
27:58.630 --> 28:01.460
and the reinforced machine gun company to hold Luding Bridge.

496
28:01.460 --> 28:03.410
Li's Battalion is deployed in the town.

497
28:03.130 --> 28:06.500
[Li Jinshan, Commander of the 38th Regiment, 4th Brigade]

498
28:03.790 --> 28:05.700
Even if the Communist Army had wings,

499
28:05.700 --> 28:07.030
they couldn't fly over.

500
28:07.070 --> 28:08.550
Very good, Regiment Commander Li.

501
28:08.550 --> 28:09.700
If you hold Luding Bridge,

502
28:09.700 --> 28:11.100
you will have done a great deed.

503
28:11.100 --> 28:11.860
Yes, sir!

504
28:14.780 --> 28:15.500
Come on.

505
28:15.580 --> 28:16.600
My turn.

506
28:42.120 --> 28:45.720
Company Commander, the Communist Army opposite us is scouting.

507
28:49.940 --> 28:52.070
Listen up, Communist Army over there!

508
28:52.630 --> 28:55.070
I'm quite comfortable right now.

509
28:55.390 --> 28:56.910
Don't bother me!

510
28:57.180 --> 28:59.660
Let's see you fly over here!

511
28:59.980 --> 29:02.980
Then I'll lay down my arms and surrender immediately!

512
29:06.590 --> 29:07.520
Don't shoot.

513
29:07.720 --> 29:08.590
Save your ammo.

514
29:13.020 --> 29:14.750
Why are you getting mad at them?

515
29:16.020 --> 29:17.750
Sichuan Army on the other side,

516
29:17.830 --> 29:19.310
listen to me!

517
29:19.590 --> 29:20.940
Your Red Army grandpas

518
29:21.310 --> 29:22.910
not only want your guns,

519
29:23.460 --> 29:24.870
but also your bridge!

520
29:25.220 --> 29:26.830
I'll take your bridge first,

521
29:27.150 --> 29:28.530
then disarm you!

522
29:28.830 --> 29:30.160
Did you hear me clearly?

523
29:31.260 --> 29:34.350
Anyone can brag and talk big.

524
29:34.870 --> 29:37.110
If you think you can, fly over here!

525
29:37.500 --> 29:39.220
And I'll chat with you.

526
29:39.590 --> 29:41.280
I'll even sing you an opera.

527
29:45.740 --> 29:46.420
The 1st Division on the opposite bank

528
29:46.420 --> 29:47.840
is blocked by the enemy at Tiesigou.

529
29:47.840 --> 29:50.700
We can only rely on ourselves to take Luding Bridge.

530
29:59.560 --> 30:01.020
Then there's no other way.

531
30:01.260 --> 30:02.550
We can only force an attack.

532
30:02.550 --> 30:04.500
Yes. We launch a frontal assault and strike fast.

533
30:04.500 --> 30:06.300
We have to fight our way through.

534
30:07.980 --> 30:08.940
My suggestion is

535
30:09.390 --> 30:11.260
that the 1st Battalion form a commando team to attack forward.

536
30:11.260 --> 30:12.350
The remaining companies

537
30:12.350 --> 30:13.620
will lay planks while attacking

538
30:13.620 --> 30:14.790
to take the bridgehead.

539
30:14.790 --> 30:17.260
The 2nd and 3rd Battalions will concentrate all firepower

540
30:17.260 --> 30:18.910
to block the enemy reinforcements.

541
30:18.910 --> 30:20.220
After taking Luding Bridge,

542
30:20.220 --> 30:22.660
we will concentrate our forces to take Luding Town.

543
30:22.660 --> 30:23.380
Agreed.

544
30:29.540 --> 30:30.280
Liao Dazhu!

545
30:30.610 --> 30:31.350
Here!

546
30:32.420 --> 30:33.350
Liu Jinshan!

547
30:33.660 --> 30:34.460
Here!

548
30:34.200 --> 30:35.330
[Liao Dazhu, Company Commander of the 2nd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

549
30:35.180 --> 30:36.110
Wang Haiyun!

550
30:35.330 --> 30:36.470
[and Commando Team Leader]

551
30:36.220 --> 30:37.180
Yes!

552
30:37.740 --> 30:38.840
[Liu Jinshan, Party Branch Secretary of the 3rd Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Red Army Corps,]

553
30:38.220 --> 30:39.020
Li Youlin!

554
30:38.840 --> 30:39.950
[and Commando Team Political Instructor]

555
30:39.220 --> 30:40.150
Here!

556
30:40.350 --> 30:41.260
Liu Zihua!

557
30:41.390 --> 30:42.180
Here!

558
30:42.980 --> 30:43.780
Zhao Changfa!

559
30:43.870 --> 30:44.700
Here!

560
30:45.290 --> 30:46.150
Yang Tianming!

561
30:46.180 --> 30:47.180
Here!

562
30:47.700 --> 30:48.500
Wei Xiaosan!

563
30:48.910 --> 30:49.630
Here!

564
30:51.020 --> 30:51.880
Wang Hongshan!

565
30:51.990 --> 30:52.820
Here!

566
30:54.180 --> 30:54.960
Liu Dagui!

567
30:54.980 --> 30:55.910
Here!

568
30:58.770 --> 30:59.730
Li Furen!

569
30:59.880 --> 31:00.770
Here!

570
31:32.590 --> 31:33.660
Yun Guichuan!

571
31:34.310 --> 31:35.420
Here!

572
31:36.050 --> 31:38.080
Yun Guichuan, when climbing the iron chains,

573
31:38.080 --> 31:39.100
don't stick your butt out.

574
31:39.100 --> 31:39.830
Watch out for bullets.

575
31:39.830 --> 31:41.230
Company Commander, I'll remember.

576
31:41.230 --> 31:42.790
Don't give me that silly grin.

577
31:42.790 --> 31:43.650
Keep it in mind.

578
31:43.680 --> 31:45.080
Yes, Company Commander!

579
31:45.310 --> 31:46.230
Go ahead.

580
31:56.640 --> 31:57.530
Everyone,

581
31:57.740 --> 31:58.770
change gear quickly.

582
31:58.770 --> 31:59.610
Yes, sir!

583
32:01.510 --> 32:02.640
Double time, march!

584
32:50.300 --> 32:51.080
Comrades.

585
32:52.220 --> 32:53.350
Have you heard about

586
32:53.500 --> 32:55.260
the 1st Regiment's forced crossing of the Dadu River

587
32:55.260 --> 32:56.260
a few days ago?

588
32:56.260 --> 32:57.550
We have!

589
32:58.830 --> 33:00.590
Our comrades in the 1st Regiment

590
33:00.590 --> 33:02.180
were able to tear a hole

591
33:02.180 --> 33:04.380
in the enemy's Dadu River defense line.

592
33:04.500 --> 33:06.500
Can our comrades in the 4th Regiment

593
33:06.500 --> 33:08.870
break through the natural barrier of Luding Bridge

594
33:08.870 --> 33:11.940
and open a path for the CPC Central Committee and the main force?

595
33:11.940 --> 33:14.590
Yes! Yes! Yes!

596
33:15.730 --> 33:17.980
This is what the Red Army should look like.

597
33:17.980 --> 33:20.420
This is what a vanguard regiment should look like.

598
33:20.420 --> 33:21.500
Comrades!

599
33:21.790 --> 33:22.920
Prepare for battle!

600
33:22.940 --> 33:24.180
Yes, sir!

601
35:14.150 --> 35:15.150
Get on the bridge.

602
36:07.020 --> 36:08.160
Hurry!

603
36:54.310 --> 36:55.640
The Communist Army is crossing the bridge!

604
36:55.640 --> 36:57.100
The Communist Army is crossing the bridge!

605
36:57.100 --> 36:59.500
The Communist Army is crossing the bridge!

606
37:04.670 --> 37:05.190
Fire!

607
37:05.320 --> 37:06.680
Fire! Fire!

608
37:08.240 --> 37:09.200
Shoot!

609
37:53.610 --> 37:54.690
Shoot!

610
38:36.680 --> 38:39.080
Artillery Company, support! Hurry!

611
38:39.420 --> 38:40.110
Yes, sir!

612
39:55.710 --> 39:57.970
Suppress the enemy's firing positions!

613
40:32.310 --> 40:35.100
Yun Guichuan, don't let go!

614
40:35.260 --> 40:37.050
Don't let go!

615
40:41.580 --> 40:43.750
Come up!

616
40:59.140 --> 41:00.420
Yun Guichuan!

617
41:01.350 --> 41:02.480
Hold on!

618
41:26.230 --> 41:27.880
Keep moving forward!

619
41:49.750 --> 41:52.010
Brigade Commander! Brigade Commander!

620
41:55.750 --> 41:57.350
The Communist Army has launched an all-out assault!

621
41:57.350 --> 41:59.020
I request reinforcements!

622
42:00.980 --> 42:03.540
I'm also under attack by the Communist Army on the east bank!

623
42:03.540 --> 42:04.470
I can't help you!

624
42:05.600 --> 42:06.260
Brigade...

625
42:10.680 --> 42:11.840
Darn it!

626
42:18.310 --> 42:19.230
Set the fire!

627
42:19.620 --> 42:20.350
Set the fire!

628
42:20.520 --> 42:21.000
Go!

629
42:21.030 --> 42:22.490
Pour the kerosene! Hurry!

630
42:22.930 --> 42:23.850
Hurry up!

631
42:24.570 --> 42:25.410
Hurry!

632
42:33.200 --> 42:33.910
Shoot!
